--6869a"></div><div class=3D"index-module--postContent--f670e"><p>Some UI u=
pdates should be performed as quickly as possible (typing into an input fie=
ld, select a value from dropdown), while others can have lower priority (fi=
ltering a list).</p>
<p>Until now, React hasn't provided a tool to prioritize UI updates.</p>
<p>Fortunately, starting React 18 (which is in alpha as of June 2021) you c=
an enable the concurrent mode =E2=80=94 which allows you to mark
UI updates as high or interruptible-low priority.</p>
<p>In this post, you'll learn how to use <code>useTransition()</code> hook =
to mark UI updates as low priority, which is especially useful for heavy no=
n-urgent updates.</p>
