<p><a href=3D"https://codesandbox.io/s/heavy-update-as-urgent-ejwbg?file=3D=
/src/FilterList.js" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">Open the =
demo.</a></p>
<p><code>&lt;FilterList names=3D{names} /&gt;</code> accepts a big array of=
 names. Inside of the component, <code>query</code> is the state variable t=
hat contains the query string. The input field is a <a href=3D"https://dmit=
ripavlutin.com/controlled-inputs-using-react-hooks/">controlled
component</a> that updates <code>query</code> state variable when the user =
types.</p>
<p>Open the <a href=3D"https://dmitripavlutin.com/react-usetransition/(http=
s://codesandbox.io/s/heavy-update-as-urgent-ejwbg?file=3D/src/FilterList.js=
)">demo</a> and quickly type a query into the input field. You would notice=
 typing lags and the UI feels unresponsive for noticeable periods.</p>
<p>Why does it happen, and how to solve it?</p>
<p>Updating the input field value when the user types is an urgent task tha=
t must perform fast. However, updating the list by highlighting the matches=
 is a heavy but non-urgent task.</p>
<p><em>The heavy non-urgent task slows down the light urgent task.</em></p>
<p><code>useTransition()</code> hook can help you separate urgent from non-=
urgent UI updates.</p>
